.Dd September 29, 2026
.Dt MAC_NETBYLABEL 4
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm mac_netbylabel
.Nd "network access control by veriexec label"
.Sh SYNOPSIS
To load the policy at boot time, place the following lines in
.Xr loader.conf 5 :
.Bd -ragged -offset indent
.Dl mac_veriexec_load="YES"
.Dl mac_netbylabel_load="YES"
.Ed
.Sh DESCRIPTION
The
.Nm
policy restricts a process's use of the
.Tn IP
network based on the
.Xr mac_veriexec 4
label of the executable the process is running.
It is a companion to
.Xr mac_veriexec 4 ,
which establishes a verified binary's identity and label;
.Nm
acts on that label to allow or deny the binary's network access.
.Pp
A verified binary's veriexec label may carry
.Dq Li net/
tokens:
.Bl -tag -width ".Li net/allow" -offset indent
.It Li net/allow
The binary is permitted to use the IP network.
.It Li net/deny
The binary is denied the IP network.
.El
.Pp
Labels are assigned in the veriexec manifest, for example:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
usr/sbin/ntpd    sha256=... label=net/allow
.Ed
.Pp
The policy is evaluated at
.Xr connect 2
and
.Xr bind 2
for
.Dv AF_INET
and
.Dv AF_INET6
sockets only.
The decision is a property of the binary a process is currently
running (its text vnode) and is re-evaluated at each
.Xr execve 2 ;
there is no process-tree inheritance.
Inbound connections are unaffected, as
.Xr accept 2
is not mediated.
.Pp
The policy is controlled through the
.Xr sysctl 8
interface:
.Bl -tag -width ".Va security.mac.netbylabel.block_loopback"
.It Va security.mac.netbylabel.enabled
Master switch.
When 0 (the default) the policy performs no checks.
.It Va security.mac.netbylabel.default_deny
When 0 (the default) the policy is a deny-list: only binaries labeled
.Li net/deny
are blocked.
When 1 it is an allow-list: every binary is blocked unless it is labeled
.Li net/allow .
.It Va security.mac.netbylabel.block_loopback
When 0 (the default) connections and binds to loopback addresses
.Pq Li 127.0.0.0/8 , Li ::1
are exempt, so the policy affects off-host traffic only.
When 1 the policy applies to loopback as well.
.El
.Pp
All three may be set as tunables in
.Xr loader.conf 5 .
Leaving loopback exempt allows name resolution through a local
resolver and local socket services to keep working for otherwise
network-denied binaries.
.Pp
A process that is denied the network by
.Nm
receives
.Er EACCES
from
.Xr connect 2
or
.Xr bind 2 .
A binary that has no veriexec label, or is not known to veriexec, is
treated as carrying no
.Li net/
token.
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr connect 2 ,
.Xr execve 2 ,
.Xr mac 4 ,
.Xr mac_veriexec 4 ,
.Xr loader.conf 5 ,
.Xr sysctl 8 ,
.Xr veriexec 8
.Sh HISTORY
The
.Nm
policy first appeared in
.Fx 15.2 .
.Sh AUTHORS
.An Quentin Thebault
